{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 132, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the edge was absent opens a new node2->output path, so the gain should beat swapping out an existing skip, pool or conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 gets no input, so adding the conv also brings edges 2 and 4 back into use."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input->node2 edge adds capacity and a new path, while replacing an existing op gains only marginally."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the node1->node2 conv deepens the cell when that edge was missing, which helps more than upgrading an op already there."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on an empty node1->output edge contributes a new feature path into the output."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input->output residual where none existed greatly eases optimization of the stacked network, more than swapping it in for another op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, removing edge 3 leaves edge 5 as the only route into the output, so the loss is larger."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the residual skip, removing edge 5 takes away a larger share of the signal reaching the output."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "